| 18a | AFTER | `C16` a clock decides a document's arrival: the island's slot wait and the bounded find. MET LIVE on 2026-11-19: the operator's house refused every compose after a lock and unlock, and on a fresh `up`, at `wikis/lares/personal` (`never arrived over syncPort`, 8614 ms of port silence), the island waiting on its own store behind the rest guard's ask to the vessel (lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/research/stable-house #/the-fault). PARTLY BUILT: Relock-Mender's cure (PR #316) pauses the silence clock while the island's own store holds a read in flight and names the store in the fault, and the meshpalace map stops minting a document at every compose (PR #317). Owed: road (b), wiki islands keeping no store of their own (Lares-Awakens' pool), and C16's wait ending on the store's own events; until (b) lands, `vault lock` stays unrun on the live house (handoff #/alpha) | A face switch refused once under machine load on a document that stood on disk the whole time, so a wall clock, and never the store's own state, decided who wears a face; it sits beside the epoch burn since both break the no-clocks law (#/rulings, 2026-11-06 and 2026-11-11), and it waits on `M6`'s sweep for its design. |

